    fill: all cells either YELLOW or one marker color; marker color != YELLOW
    markers:
      count: 1-5 per block (= expansion padding distance)
      placement: strictly interior (never on block border row/col)
      color: one non-yellow non-black color per block; unique across blocks [observed]
  expansion:
    each block bbox expands by pad cells on all 4 sides
    expanded bboxes must stay within grid bounds (margin >= 0)
    expanded bboxes must not overlap (gap >= 0 on each axis)
  output:
    expanded rectangles filled with marker color
    original block cells (yellow + markers) restored on top

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose square grid size 25-29.
    2. Pick N=2-3 blocks. For each, choose dimensions h(3-8) x w(3-10) and pad(1-5).
       Ensure pad <= (h-2)*(w-2) so markers fit in interior.
    3. Compute expanded bbox sizes (h+2*pad) x (w+2*pad). Place expanded bboxes
       on grid with no overlap and all within bounds. This is the hard constraint
       so place expanded boxes first via greedy or rejection.
    4. Assign distinct non-yellow non-black marker colors to each block.
    5. Build input: place yellow blocks at center of each expanded bbox.
       Scatter exactly pad marker-color pixels at random interior positions of each block.
    6. Fill rest of grid with BLACK.
